---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import MarketingChrome from "../../components/MarketingChrome.astro";

const phoneDisplay = "(501) 413-3386";
const tel = "tel:+15014133386";
const sms = "sms:+15014133386";
---

<Base
  title='Mobile Mechanic Website, Free Demo Before You Pay | NV Labs'
  description='Get found for "mobile mechanic near me." I build your free demo site with services, service area, and a call button. Call or text (501) 413-3386.'
  image="/og.png"
  robots="index, follow"
>
  <MarketingChrome>
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Mobile mechanic websites</p>
      <h1 id="hero-title">A website that gets your phone ringing for mobile repair jobs</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Free demo first. Services, service area, and a one-tap call button so people searching
        "mobile mechanic near me" can reach you fast.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-cta">
        <a class="btn btn-accent btn-lg" href={tel}>Call {phoneDisplay}</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href={sms}>Text me</a>
        <a class="btn btn-text" href="/aaron-the-mechanic/">See a mechanic demo</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="phone-title">
      <h2 id="phone-title">When a car won't start, people grab their phone</h2>
      <p>
        Nobody plans to need a mechanic. Their car dies in a parking lot or the battery quits in the
        driveway. They search "mobile mechanic near me" and call the first one that looks legit.
      </p>
      <p>
        A clean website helps you look like that legit choice. It tells them who you are, what you
        fix, and where you go, in about ten seconds.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="area-title">
      <h2 id="area-title">Your service area, front and center</h2>
      <p>
        The first question every caller asks is "Do you come out to me?" Your site answers it before
        they call.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'll add a clear service area section listing the towns and neighborhoods you cover, plus
        any spots you don't. This also helps Google understand where to show you.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="fix-title">
      <h2 id="fix-title">What you fix on site</h2>
      <p>People want to know if their problem is something you can handle in a driveway. I'll lay out your jobs in plain words, like:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Battery testing and replacement</li>
        <li>Brake pads and rotors</li>
        <li>Starters and alternators</li>
        <li>Oil changes and fluid checks</li>
        <li>Check engine light diagnostics</li>
        <li>No-start troubleshooting</li>
        <li>Belts, hoses, and spark plugs</li>
      </ul>
      <p>You tell me what you do and don't do, and I'll write it up.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="tap-title">
      <h2 id="tap-title">One tap to call</h2>
      <p>
        Most of your work comes from phone calls, so your site is built around one big button: call
        me. On a phone, it dials you in one tap. I can also add a short "describe the problem" form
        for people who'd rather text.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="maps-title">
      <h2 id="maps-title">Showing up on Google Maps</h2>
      <p>
        For searches like "mobile mechanic near me," your Google Business Profile matters a lot.
        Your website backs it up. I'll make sure your name, phone, service area, and hours match
        everywhere, and that your site links to your profile and vice versa. No guarantees on
        rankings, but you'll be set up properly.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="decide-title">
      <h2 id="decide-title">I build it first, you decide</h2>
      <p>
        I make a free demo of your site with your name, your services, and your area. You check it
        out on your phone. Like it? I put it live. Don't? No problem.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
      <h2 id="faq-title">FAQ</h2>
      <div class="faq">
        <div>
          <h3>I don't have a shop address. Is that okay?</h3>
          <p>
            Totally fine. Lots of mobile mechanics work from home or a truck. Your site can show a
            service area instead of a street address.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Can people book a time through the site?</h3>
          <p>
            Yes, if you want that. Some mechanics prefer a simple request form so they can call back
            and quote. I'll set it up the way you like to work.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>I'm under the hood all day. Will I need to update the site?</h3>
          <p>
            Not much. Once it's set up, it mostly runs on its own. If something changes, like a new
            service, just text me.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="cta-title">
      <h2 id="cta-title">Let's get your phone ringing</h2>
      <p>I'll build your demo first. Take a look when you're on a break.</p>
      <a class="phone-big" href={tel}>{phoneDisplay}</a>
      <div class="hero-cta">
        <a class="btn btn-accent btn-lg" href={tel}>Call</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href={sms}>Text</a>
      </div>
      <a class="back-home" href="/">Back to NV Labs home</a>
    </section>
  </MarketingChrome>
</Base>
